  subsets with the same final bound; unsupported target drift fails closed.
  Five cases cover identity, exact coarsening, missing-bound rejection,
  overflow-bound rejection, and normalization before same-schema merge.

  Exact refinement requires an additional caller-supplied sample witness. The
  finer histogram is rebuilt from those samples, then coarsened to the source
  schema and required to equal every source count, total, extremum, and overflow
  value. Persisted histogram state alone still cannot invent a finer
  distribution. Three cases cover valid refinement, incomplete witness, and a
  target schema that omits a source boundary.

  A pure common-schema derivation intersects two ordered schemas when their
  final overflow boundary matches. It
  returns the greatest exact shared bounds plus per-side removal counts; four
